# Working on AgentFlow

Use domain-first MVI with typed commands. Read the complete behavior and owner
boundaries in [docs/CONTRACT.md](docs/CONTRACT.md) before editing. Do not maintain
a second description of those rules here or in a new instruction file.

- Trace Action → Store → reducer → Command → runner/port → result Action.
  Change the smallest complete owner and its required consumers.
- Preserve public declarations, conformances, encoding and execution semantics.
  Search current consumers, but do not infer that an unused public API is dead.
  Follow [README versioning](README.md#versioning) before proposing a break.
- Keep one runtime, five source responsibilities and explicit dependencies.
  Add an abstraction only when an actual shared contract requires it.
- Preserve the manifest's tools/language/deployment floors. New APIs require
  support evidence; the development machine's SDK alone is insufficient.
- For runtime changes, use focused, continuation-controlled cancellation,
  stale-delivery and lifetime regressions. A runner's return handshake does not
  prove the Store has processed its completion.
- Report source changes, executed checks and unverified boundaries separately.
  Package evidence does not qualify an application or external adapter.

Installation and the single pinned package rule are in [README](README.md#install).
